# Onion architecture

- Controllers (`Journeys.API`): no business logic. Validate, call services, map HTTP.
- Services (`Journeys.Core`): all business logic; interfaces in `Interfaces/Services`.
- Persistence (`Journeys.DAL`): only data access; injected into services.
- Controller in/out types: `Journeys.DTO` only.
- External systems (Cosmos, blob, auth, bus, Backend.*): `Journeys.Infra*` only, behind interfaces.
- Every business operation is tenant-scoped (`TenantId`).
- Do not delete existing comments without cause.
- `Journeys.UX` is the HTTP-only Next.js UI. Do not project-reference Core/DAL/Infra from it. Do not put a web frontend inside the C# onion projects.
- If this solution stores user-boundary data, use a full local onion.
- Prefer DDD in one modular monolith; do not create a microservice per noun.
- `Journeys.DTO` is required.
- See `docs/platform/overlays.md` for Adapter names.
